 ```
 
+Compound duration sums can be parsed with `parseCompound`. Each term must include
+a unit, and terms are separated by one or more ASCII spaces.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms';
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m');       // 5400000
+parseCompound('-2 days 4 hours'); // -187200000
+```
+
+`parseCompound` accepts the same case-insensitive unit spellings and numeric
+syntax as `parse`, including months and years. A leading minus applies to the
+whole sum. Malformed nonempty input returns `NaN`; non-string, empty, and input
+longer than 100 characters throw an error. Compound syntax is specific to
+`parseCompound` and is not accepted by `parse`, `parseStrict`, or `ms`.
+
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
 
 If you want strict type checking for the input value, you can use `parseStrict`.
